# L §5.14.3 and E §5: pay[] didn't exist at its booking cut (ok false), so it counts as A0 = 0 (E §5 step 1); v2
# (known 2026-02-10) makes it exist, an adjustment of its cash leg by 100.00 PLN (step 3: δ = Aᵥ). arr fulfils it
# with a leg whose ends are written a.adjusts.cash.from / .to, as L §6.5 change 3 writes a settlement's place: the
# adjusted leg's places (zus -> konto), so the leg runs the adjusted leg's way and counts +100.00 PLN (step 5); the
# remainder is 0, so no HOLE-CHANGED. flows(pay, 2026) is A0 plus the settlements dated in its span (step 6,
# L §5.14.3 'settlements included'): 0 + 100.00 PLN; flows(konto, 2026) counts arr's leg into konto: 100.00 PLN.
# (Was: the HOLE-CHANGED question, since reading a leg of the instance refused RUN-NONE; a fault found by running
# a text.)
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-02-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-03-31
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind pays: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place zus: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input ok: bool
input d1: date
input d2: date
move pay: pays
  on d1
  when ok
  leg cash from zus to konto amount amt
move arr[a in adjustments on d2 where a.adjusts in pays]: pays
  on d2
  at a.day
  leg cash from a.adjusts.cash.from to a.adjusts.cash.to amount max(a.change, 0)
  fulfils a
source s "x"
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100
  ok = false
  d1 = 2026-01-05
  d2 = 2026-02-10
  opening[konto] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-02-10
  replace ok = true
ask q: flows(pay, 2026) law cut
ask k: flows(konto, 2026) law cut
=== expect
k: 100.00 PLN
  law date 2026-02-10, cut 2026-02-10
q: 100.00 PLN
  law date 2026-02-10, cut 2026-02-10
